        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "530adb4a-825f-5ede-b24a-27c8a393f350",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Little Missouri River, Missouri River, Devils Tower, Bear Lodge Mountains, Black Hills, Belle Fourche River, Crook County, Hulett, Sundance, Wyoming, Montana, South Dakota, United States\n- Concepts: tributaries, river courses, laccolithic buttes, igneous rock\n\nFacts:\n- The Little Missouri River is a 560-mile (901 km) tributary of the Missouri River in the northern Great Plains of the United States.\n- The Little Missouri River rises in northeastern Wyoming in western Crook County about 15 miles (24 km) west of Devils Tower.\n- The Little Missouri River flows northeast across a corner of southeastern Montana and into South Dakota.\n- Devils Tower, also called Bear Lodge Butte, is a laccolithic butte composed of igneous rock in the Bear Lodge Mountains, part of the Black Hills, in Crook County, northeastern Wyoming.\n- Devils Tower is near Hulett and Sundance and stands above the Belle Fourche River.\n- Devils Tower rises 1,267 feet (386 m) above the Belle Fourche River and measures 867 feet (265 m) from base to summit.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
